<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>SubgenAI.SerenityStar.Core</PackageId>
    <AssemblyName>SerenityStar.Core</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>SerenityStar</RootNamespace>
    <Description>Core client for the Serenity Star .NET SDK: authentication, error handling and file upload. Install SubgenAI.SerenityStar.SDK (agents) and/or SubgenAI.SerenityStar.AIServices instead of referencing this package directly.</Description>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageTags>ai;sdk;serenity;serenitystar</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
      Version 3.0.0 - Package split

      NEW FEATURES:
      - New package containing SerenityClient, SerenityClientBuilder, SerenityApiException and the
        AddSerenityStar dependency injection registration shared by the agents and AI services packages.
      - File upload: client.GetFileClient() returns an IFileClient to upload files (UploadAsync) or upload them
        from a public URL (UploadFromUrlAsync) and get their id, to use with the AI services *ByFileIdAsync
        methods or volatile knowledge UploadFromFileForAgentAsync. AddSerenityStar registers IFileClient.
      - Typed API errors, shared by every feature package: SerenityApiException.Error is a SerenityApiError
        (namespace SerenityStar.Errors.Models) with Code, Message, DocumentationUrl, RetryAfter and ExtensionData
        * Typed by code: InputValidationError, ValidationError, ResourceNotFoundError, RateLimitExceededError,
          AgentExecutionFailedError and AIServiceExecutionFailedError. Other codes use SerenityApiError itself
        * AgentExecutionFailedError and AIServiceExecutionFailedError list every attempt made against the AI provider
          (Attempts, or Files for OCR), with its code, raw provider status and provider detail (VendorError)
        * RetryAfter is read from the Retry-After header on HTTP responses, and from retry_after_seconds on streaming
          error events
        * Fields this SDK version doesn't model yet are kept in ExtensionData
        * Constants for codes and keys (namespace SerenityStar.Errors.Constants): SerenityErrorCodes, VendorErrorCodes,
          ValidationErrorKeys, ResourceNotFoundKeys and AgentModelTypes

      BREAKING CHANGES:
      - AddSerenityStar now throws ArgumentNullException at registration when the API key is null or empty,
        instead of failing on the first request. Apps that register with an empty key (e.g. tests or
        design-time tooling) now fail at startup.
      - SerenityApiException moved from SerenityStar.Exceptions to SerenityStar.Errors, and now exposes the parsed error
        * ReasonPhrase and ResponseJson (3.0.0-beta1) are replaced by Error (the SerenityApiError) and ResponseContent
          (the raw body, set only when it isn't a Serenity API error)
        * Exception.Message is now the error message returned by the API, instead of "Request failed with status code X"
        * It still derives from HttpRequestException, so existing catch (HttpRequestException) blocks keep working
      - Requires the Serenity Star API error format with error codes. Errors without a code read as
        SerenityErrorCodes.Unknown

      SECURITY:
      - Logging a whole error object can log user input and model output, such as ValidationError.GeneratedJson.
        Log Code, Message and DocumentationUrl instead, or treat those logs as sensitive.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- Feature packages need the internal authenticated API client. Never add assemblies outside this solution. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SerenityStar" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SerenityStar.AIServices" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Http" Version="6.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Options" Version="6.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection.Abstractions" Version="6.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Net.Http.Json" Version="8.0.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="8.0.5" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
